    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.27868v1</id>
    <title>Integrating Generative Artificial Intelligence with Learning Style Models: Opportunities, Challenges, and Future Directions</title>
    <updated>2026-11-20T17:14:52Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.27868v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.27868v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Generative Artificial Intelligence (Generative AI) has emerged as a powerful tool for transforming learning. This review examines how Generative AI can be integrated with established learning style models (VARK, Kolb, Felder-Silverman, and Honey &amp; Mumford) to support student engagement in large online classes. Following PRISMA 2020 guidelines, we searched Scopus, IEEE Xplore, and Google Scholar (2015 to 2026) and included 41 studies that met the eligibility criteria. The review maps Generative AI capabilities to learning style preferences, synthesizes existing implementations, highlights benefits and challenges, and proposes pathways for future research and practice. Despite ongoing debates regarding the empirical validity of learning styles, Generative AI enables flexible, multimodal, and real-time adaptation. This study offers practical insights for educators and developers seeking to build more effective, learner centered learning systems</summary>
    <category term="cs.AI" scheme="http://arxiv.org/schemas/atom"/>
