    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2611.27743v1</id>
    <title>Pre-Crawl Prioritization and Seed Classification for Large-Scale Web Archiving</title>
    <updated>2026-11-20T15:37:26Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.27743v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.27743v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Pre-crawl prioritization systems decide which pages to fetch first before indexing, aiming to improve crawl efficiency and coverage. Existing approaches based on page popularity and relevance are unsuited to web-archival crawlers that prioritize comprehensive coverage over selective retrieval. We explore prioritization techniques tailored to web archival operations using URL lexical analysis, dynamic domain reputation systems, and HTTP response analysis to inform crawl scheduling decisions. By incorporating predictive models that estimate content change and disappearance probabilities, we improve crawl completeness while reducing redundant visits to stable resources. Through large-scale experiments, we demonstrate that our methods improve archival effectiveness and resource utilization compared to undirected crawling.</summary>
